            <ArticleTitle>Headache following epidural analgesia.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>79-80</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Many headaches following epidural analgesia are a consequence of a dural tap having occurred. However, this is not always the case and careful evaluation is required. A case of postpartum headache caused by an intracerebral haemorrhage is presented.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
